Well, the local games folks installed NetHack on a computer that's got more
reasonable limits on games usage (in fact, the computer's dedicated to
gaming-- cool!) so I've been able to play NetHack a bit more than I could
on the account I compiled it in.  (I started running out of space for level
files; the storage was pretty tight.)  I've been playing Tourists, natch;
they're my favorite class, even if they are kind of wimpy (though a first-
level WoW, giving me GDSM, Vorpal Blade, and an AoLS, certainly fixed *that*
problem) and their quest is cute!  (I dropped by in Wizard mode to see what
it was.)  So here are some more comments, and some followups on my initial
comments:

* Well, that first-level wand of wishing did come in really handy, so I
  guess I'm not *too* cheezed about the first-level WoD.  Not like I
  invested a lot of effort in the character, I guess.  Still, shouldn't
  we get points for being killed in such a flamboyant manner?  Sort of
  like "Paranoia" players get a round of applause when one of their clones
  gets vaporized?  (:3

* I tested in wizard mode, forcing the gods to be pleased, and they *still*
  wouldn't cure my blindness.  This seems like a bug to me; what's the point
  of divine intervention if they don't think blindness is a problem?

* I do hope that - key problem will be fixed in NH3.1.2...

* I love the LOS routines for the town watchmen.  Tres realistique.  And
  fun to have to wait for them to move someplace before picking that lock.

* I bought out the candle shop, and trekked to my altar to identify the
  candles.  I had four uncursed candles, two uncursed candles, and two
  blessed candles.  Can candles have plusses or something?  (They wouldn't
  combine into one slot.)  And do I need to get at least seven in one slot
  to load the Candelabra?

* Monsters are still suckers for traps.  Some of them should be smarter
  than beelining for you.  In fact, some of them, if it's not already
  implemented, should go around things to get at you if they know where
  you are.

* I still don't like certain details about the blindness implementations.
  But you've heard me grouse about that before.

* I still want to be able to attack doors and statues!  Make some use out
  of Vorpal Blade besides turning monsters into so much vat gruel.

* I really hope the sleep dichotomy gets fixed in NH3.1.2.  I really do.

* If you get bashed or something while putting on armor, or doing other
  stuff, you should be given the option of stopping or continuing.  At
  present, it isn't consistent; armor you keep putting on, for instance,
  while tins you stop opening.  (Side note: uncursed tins are a pain when
  you're fainting.  You can't get them open.  Can't they be partially
  opened?  Like partially eaten, but just for tins?)

* I am *really sick* of discovering a falling-rock trap and knowing my pet
  is doomed.  If I've discovered a trap, my pet should either automatically
  avoid it, or at least I should be able to warn it or something.  (The
  first is probably a lot easier to implement.)

* Odd thing noticed: when you use detect items, you detect items being
  carried.  Makes a nice way to spot fleeing leprechauns.

* A nymph swiped something from me while I was encumbered, and it took a
  turn for that to be reflected in my statistics.  (She'd taken me down a
  weight level.)  This should be fixed.

* Can doors be cursed?  I remember one game where my dog simply would not
  follow me through a certain door.  I had to drop a tripe ration beyond
  it, let her walk through, then block the doorway with my body and herd
  her down the alley.  (Other odd thought: do pets have sexes?  Prolly
  doesn't matter, but I like to give my pets girl names.)

* What the heck are shriekers, anyway?  They don't do damage, they don't
  kill attributes... do they curse or something?

Enough for now.  See you on the Astral Plane!

